LI installer and generated config, the MCPB manifest, the MySQL demo config (`examples/mysql-demo/sqllens.toml`), and the standalone Ant"}, {"file": "docs/internal/agent/factory.md", "line": 173, "text": "Any other scheme raises `ValueError` (`unsupported database scheme: \u2026 (expected mysql)`). Config loading already refuses every scheme other than `mysql` and `my"}, {"file": "docs/internal/agent/factory.md", "line": 177, "text": "`sqlglot_dialect_for_url(url)` (in `sqllens.safety`) maps the same scheme to a sqlglot dialect name (`\"mysql\"`, or `None` for any other scheme) that `build_agen"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 11, "text": "1. **Parser guard** \u2014 `assert_select_only` / `ReadOnlyGuardRunner` rejects anything that isn't a single `SELECT` / `WITH` (plus an allowlist of structural read-"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 38, "text": "7. **Reject side-effecting / DoS / RCE functions.** A syntactically valid `SELECT` can still call `load_file` (MySQL data exfiltration) or `SLEEP(60)` (MySQL Do"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 61, "text": "- **Schema introspection.** The guard is write-protection, not access control: a plain `SELECT` against a system catalog (`information_schema.*`, `mysql.*`) is "}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 76, "text": "`_CATALOGS_BY_DIALECT` has one entry, `mysql`; with `dialect=None`, or a dialect with no entry, the union of every entry applies, which is the same four schemas"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 117, "text": "- **SQL execution.** The MySQL runner's `run_sql` coroutine hands its synchronous driver work (`connect`, the row-level-security relation check that `require_ba"}, {"file": "docs/internal/setup/preflight.md", "line": 54, "text": "A URL with no `://` separator fails fast with `database.url is missing the '://' separator`, and a scheme that does not start with `mysql` (`sqlite` included) w"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 58, "text": "`Country` NVARCHAR(40),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 79, "text": "`Country` NVARCHAR(40),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 102, "text": "`BillingCountry` NVARCHAR(40),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 683, "text": "(150, N'Kill ''Em All', 50),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 689, "text": "(156, N'...And Justice For All', 50),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/Chinook_MySql.sql", "line": 766, "text": "(233, N'All That You Can''t Leave Behind', 150),"}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/README.md", "line": 29, "text": "pip install sqllens            # or, from a checkout: pip install -e \".[dev,all]\""}, {"file": "examples/mysql-demo/README.md", "line": 40, "text": "- \"What's the most popular genre by track count?\""}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/readonly.py", "line": 203, "text": "def _catalog_names(dialect: str | None) -> frozenset[str]:"}], "audit_hints_truncated": true, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-410/local-20261117T095601Z-1-shadow/view-head", "revision": "ec28dc1026778b28e91e55c6e10bf07904c98f14"}, "base": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-410/local-20261117T095601Z-1-shadow/view-base", "revision": "b1855615a8c5fec0d1944fcfc93b5fa397b5cc0e"}}, "dependency_sources": [], "pr": {"number": "410", "body": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-410/local-20261117T095601Z-1-shadow/pr-body.md", "head_ref": "worktree-issue-383-remove-sqlite", "base_ref": "main", "api_head_sha": "ec28dc1026778b28e91e55c6e10bf07904c98f14", "author_trust": "not-looked-up"}, "issue": {"number": "383", "source": "override", "context": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-410/local-20261117T095601Z-1-shadow/issue-context.md"}, "warnings": []}
